{"nodes": [{"id": "packages_db_memgraph_readme_migrate_memgraph", "label": "migrate-memgraph.ts runner", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "packages/db/memgraph/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Applies NNNN_name.cypher in lexical order over Bolt; versions are (:SchemaMigration {version, appliedAt}) nodes; 'already exists' counts as applied."}, {"id": "packages_db_memgraph_readme_graph_model", "label": "Graph model: :Ci plus type label, upper-case edge types", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "packages/db/memgraph/README.md", "source_location": "## Model", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every CI node carries :Ci and a PascalCase type label from CI_TYPES; every RELATIONSHIP_TYPES member is an upper-case edge type with direction exactly as the contract names it. Node properties mirror the Postgres cis row; attributes stay in Postgres/ClickHouse because the graph answers structure questions only."}, {"id": "packages_db_memgraph_readme_retired_removal", "label": "Retired CIs removed from graph", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "packages/db/memgraph/README.md", "source_location": "## Model", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Retired CIs and relationships are deleted from Memgraph (Postgres and ClickHouse keep them) so a traversal never filters on validTo; time-travel structure questions go to ci_history/relationship_history in ClickHouse."}, {"id": "packages_db_memgraph_readme_constraints_indexes", "label": "Memgraph constraints and indexes", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "packages/db/memgraph/README.md", "source_location": "## Constraints and indexes", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Unique c.id, existence of tenantId and type, property indexes incl. composite (tenantId, type, identityKey) for reconciliation lookups, a label index per CI type and edge-type index per relationship type so named-edge traversals never scan, :BusinessService(impactedBy) for blast-radius ranking."}, {"id": "packages_db_memgraph_readme_impact_query", "label": "Impact query shape", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "packages/db/memgraph/README.md", "source_location": "## Impact query shape", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Edges point from dependant to dependency so impact flows against the arrows: MATCH (c:Ci)<-[:DEPENDS_ON|RUNS_ON|POWERED_BY|HOSTED_ON*1..$depth]-(x)-[:PART_OF_SERVICE]->(s:BusinessService); power and rack scenarios expand the failed set first via LOCATED_IN then reuse the shape with WHERE c.id IN $ids; $depth from ImpactScenario.options.maxDepth."}, {"id": "packages_db_memgraph_readme_impacted_by_triggers", "label": "BusinessService.impactedBy triggers", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "packages/db/memgraph/README.md", "source_location": "## Triggers", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Three AFTER COMMIT triggers (edge create, edge delete, service create) maintain the count of distinct CIs whose failure reaches a service within {impact_closure_depth} hops, so the console shows blast radius per row without a traversal per row."}, {"id": "packages_db_memgraph_readme_impact_closure_depth", "label": "IMPACT_CLOSURE_DEPTH parameter", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "packages/db/memgraph/README.md", "source_location": "## Triggers", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Substituted by the runner from src/parameters.ts because a Cypher variable-length range bound must be a literal."}], "edges": [{"source": "packages_db_memgraph_readme_migrate_memgraph", "target": "deploy_compose_docker_compose_memgraph", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score